# Everything here is about the BUILD CONTEXT — the tarball the daemon receives
# before a single instruction runs. Without this file that context was the whole
# folder: ~40 MB, of which 38 MB was node_modules that the image installs itself
# anyway, plus whatever archives happened to be sitting in warcs/.

# Installed inside the image by `bun install --frozen-lockfile`. Shipping the
# host's copy is both slow and wrong — it may have been built for another
# platform.
node_modules

# Runtime data. warcs/ is mounted at runtime, and its contents are measured in
# gigabytes; nothing about it belongs in a build.
warcs/
*.warc
*.warc.gz
*.wacz

# Run output.
*.log

# Secrets. .env must never be baked into a layer — layers are readable by anyone
# who can pull the image, and deleting the file in a later step does not remove
# it from the one that added it. The values are supplied at runtime instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and caches.
out
dist
coverage
*.lcov
*.tsbuildinfo
*.tgz

# Not needed to run the server, and each one invalidates the build cache when it
# changes. The Dockerfile's own COPY is the one exception that has to stay
# visible, so it is not listed here.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
README.md
parser/*.md

# Editor and OS droppings.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
